  "html": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2223,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-09-01242025.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2223\" style=\"width:400px\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-dots\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-dots\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Weekly prompts to help you think a little harder, write a little longer, and have a bit of fun in your journal. I provide the prompt and then a bit of discussion afterward to help you think beyond the prompt.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How To Use Weekly Prompts</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Using weekly prompts can be as simple or as difficult as you would like. I do not use one every day, and sometimes I use several from the weekly prompts list at one time. Over time, I have learned that too simple doesn't work for me. I like to push the question around in my mind, look at it from a couple of different perspectives, and see what comes out.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Imagine, if you will, the prompt as a unique piece of artwork. Put that piece of artwork on a pedestal and then move around it. Look from side to side, high to low, and anything between. I want it to speak to me, give me thoughts, and guide my thoughts into a deeper understanding.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>In all seriousness, I do study the question. I don't spend hours on it and sometimes not even minutes. A few seconds and a few pointed questions after. Generally, those questions begin with why. Why did the prompt spark that response? Does that matter to me, and why? Why did I choose that answer/point? My meanings and questions can be vastly different from yours. That's okay! The prompts are supposed to spark YOUR thoughts and feelings.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"textAlign\":\"left\"} -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left\">Focus Quote</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"lightbox\":{\"enabled\":true},\"id\":2224,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full is-resized\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-08-01242025.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2224\" style=\"width:400px\"/></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"28px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:28px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote {\"textAlign\":\"center\"} -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote has-text-align-center\"><!-- wp:quote -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>So I often feel like the self that I construct in writing feels truer to how I think of myself than the self I'm constructing in any other way. </em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><em>Yaa Gyasi</em></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote --></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:spacer {\"height\":\"28px\"} -->\n<div style=\"height:28px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n<!-- /wp:spacer -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>When writing, there is freedom in my thoughts and words. I can say what I want, when I want, without regard for anyone else's feelings. This results in me being fully myself at the time of writing. We spend a lot of time adjusting our tone, thoughts, and words to account for the thoughts and opinions of others. While that's okay, it also is stifling at times. There is an intense pleasure in being free to state your thoughts and opinions. For me, this only happens in the journal.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-dots\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-dots\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:shortcode -->\n<center><div data-slideshow-id=\"1546\"></div></center>\n<!-- /wp:shortcode -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-dots\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-dots\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Weekly Inspiration</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":2225,\"mediaLink\":\"https://divergentjournaler.com/?attachment_id=2225\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"imageFill\":false,\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile is-style-default\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-11-01242025.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2225 size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Journaling</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"placeholder\":\"Content…\"} -->\n<p>A cathartic journal page doesn't have to be all pretty and simple. Let those thoughts out, bits and pieces, or long flowing paragraphs. Just let it all out.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1083537991592093590/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"></a><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1083537991597862190/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1083537991587443079/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Pin by blog.pencils.com</a></a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaPosition\":\"right\",\"mediaId\":2226,\"mediaLink\":\"https://divergentjournaler.com/?attachment_id=2226\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"mediaType\":\"image\",\"mediaSizeSlug\":\"full\",\"imageFill\":false,\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text has-media-on-the-right is-stacked-on-mobile is-style-default\"><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Art Journaling</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>\"I think I think too much\" </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Art journal pages that speak to my state of mind always make me the happiest! They remind me I am not alone in my moments.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1083537991593700852/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Pin by Sabrina</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-12-01242025.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2226 size-full\"/></figure></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:media-text {\"mediaId\":2227,\"mediaLink\":\"https://divergentjournaler.com/?attachment_id=2227\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\",\"mediaType\":\"image\"} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-13-01242025.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2227 size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\"><!-- wp:heading {\"level\":4} -->\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Bullet Journaling</h4>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I love how this bullet journal page pulls together the elements of art, photos, and standard bullet journaling in a unique way.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph {\"placeholder\":\"Content…\"} -->\n<p><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/pin/1083537991592093079/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Pin by Mariko Giverink.</a></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div></div>\n<!-- /wp:media-text -->\n\n<!-- wp:quote {\"fontSize\":\"small\"} -->\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote has-small-font-size\"><!-- wp:paragraph {\"align\":\"left\",\"style\":{\"layout\":{\"selfStretch\":\"fit\",\"flexSize\":null}}} -->\n<p class=\"has-text-align-left\">The images that I choose for inspiration are not about the links. They are solely about the images and what they represent. I love seeing other people's journals. I love the inspiration that hits me to go write in my own. Sometimes, that inspiration leads me to try something I have seen on their pages. Mostly, it just inspires me to write!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></blockquote>\n<!-- /wp:quote -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Weekly Prompts</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.01 Describe your best friend. </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>How do they make you feel? Are they funny or serious? Do you laugh until you cry when you are together? Do you cry together? When your friend is hurting, do you hurt as well? Friends are a blessing in our lives. So grateful for my friends.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2228,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-01-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-01-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2228\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.02 Are you a person who is ready when tax season starts, or do you put it off until the last minute? </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Usually, I have all of my things together and prepared in December. This year, I'm not sure what happened; it's still all a mess.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2229,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-02-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-02-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2229\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.03 What is something you would like to learn more about? </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do you have a desire to learn about gardening, painting, or some other type of hobby? Perhaps an event in history interests you? I have a habit of digging into the most random of things. Today, it was the first band Chester Bennington played in and the history of highlighters. Sometimes, the rabbit holes are the best distraction.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2230,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-03-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-03-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2230\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.04 What's your pet peeve this week? </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do your pet peeves change, or are you one of those lucky people who only have a few? Mine have a habit of changing with the ebb and flow of my emotions. When I am feeling emotional, all sounds aggravate me.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2231,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-04-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-04-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2231\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.05 What's on your schedule today? </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Do you have plans? Will it be a busy day or an easy, laid-back day? Is it a dress-up-and-go kind of day, or will you hang out in your PJs all day? Maybe skip work and hang out in a hammock? So many choices, so little time. What will you choose today?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2232,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\",\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized is-style-default\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-05-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-05-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2232\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.06 If you had the power, what would you change in your life at this very moment? </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>All your past choices and events stay the same, but one magical change could be yours. Would you have a better job? Change your physical appearance? Increase the balance in your checkbook? Change your marital status? Go big or go home, right? One big change would be such a hard choice.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2233,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\",\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized is-style-default\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-06-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-06-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2233\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">56.07 Word of the week: Foppish. </h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Look it up, write it down, and use it in a sentence or two. Do you know someone who is foppish?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":2234,\"width\":\"400px\",\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"media\",\"align\":\"center\",\"className\":\"is-style-default\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-large is-resized is-style-default\"><a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-07-01242025.png\"><img src=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/dj-dialogues-07-01242025-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2234\" style=\"width:400px\"/></a></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:separator {\"className\":\"is-style-dots\"} -->\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-dots\"/>\n<!-- /wp:separator -->\n\n<!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:group {\"layout\":{\"type\":\"constrained\"}} -->\n<div class=\"wp-block-group\"><!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>I hope these weekly prompts inspire you to think harder, dig deeper, and write a little longer this week. Looking for more prompts? Check out the <a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/category/divergent-dialogues/\">Divergent Dialogues</a> category to see more weekly prompts, <a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/journal-prompts/fun-journal-prompts/\">31+ Fun Journaling Prompts</a>, or head on over to my <a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/divergentjournaler/prompts-divergentjournaler/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Pinterest board</a>!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Have you signed up for unlimited access to the <a href=\"https://divergentjournaler.com/divergent-vault/\">Divergent Vault</a>, which features over 100 free journaling printables and freebies?</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Happy Journaling!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Sarah G.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:shortcode -->\n<center><div data-slideshow-id=\"1490\"></div></center>\n<!-- /wp:shortcode --></div>\n<!-- /wp:group -->"
}